cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ClimateNetAI in your research, please cite this software."
title: "ClimateNetAI: Climate-Aware Machine Learning for Wireless Signal Prediction"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-08-11
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Michael"
    given-names: "Olohimai Juliet"
repository-code: "https://github.com/olohi184/-ClimateNetAI-"
url: "https://climatenetai.streamlit.app"
abstract: >
  ClimateNetAI is a climate-aware machine-learning research application
  for predicting wireless signal strength under atmospheric variability.
  It integrates monthly machine-learning models, validation metrics,
  model comparison and recommendation, reliability controls,
  data-quality notices, performance visualization, and downloadable
  prediction reports.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - wireless communications
  - RSSI
  - climate-aware AI
  - 5G
  - climate-resilient digital infrastructure
